  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ameresco obligated $309M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Ameresco won 36 awards this period, with an average award size of $8.6M. Ameresco's obligations are down 42.8% year over year. Ameresco's largest buyer in FY2026 to date is the Department of Veterans Affairs, which obligated $228M. The Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer, with $68.4M in obligations. Ameresco's primary market is Engineering Services, which accounted for $307M in obligations. Historical obligations show variation: FY21 was $94.1M, FY22 was $122M, FY23 was $107M, FY24 was $75.8M, and FY25 was $541M. The data reflect contract obligations; award-value figures in some tables are total contract values. Current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. Use these figures to prioritize outreach to the Department of Veterans Affairs and to position Engineering Services capabilities for federal procurements.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Ameresco's federal business changed year over year?",
        "body": "Ameresco's obligations fell 42.8% year over year. Ameresco's FY26 obligations of $309M follow FY25 obligations of $541M and earlier years of $75.8M (FY24), $107M (FY23), $122M (FY22), and $94.1M (FY21). These figures show that FY25 was an outlier high and FY26 is a partial fiscal-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Ameresco's main federal customers and markets?",
        "body": "Ameresco's top buyer in FY2026 to date is the Department of Veterans Affairs with $228M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $68.4M. Ameresco's dominant market is Engineering Services, which accounted for $307M, with smaller activity in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $1.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Ameresco make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Ameresco made $309M from federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Ameresco received 36 awards this period, with an average award size of $8.6M and obligations down 42.8% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Ameresco?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs buys the most from Ameresco, with $228M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer with $68.4M, and smaller buyers include the Department of the Interior ($6.2M), the National Archives and Records Administration ($4.5M), and the Department of Justice ($1.2M)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Ameresco sell to the government?",
      "a": "Ameresco sells Engineering Services to the government, with $307M in obligations in that market in FY2026 to date. Ameresco also has obligations in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $1.3M, plus smaller amounts in construction-related NAICS categories."
